WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.020 --> 00:00:04.580
"Siri, what's one trillion dollars to the tenth power?"

00:00:04.900 --> 00:00:12.100
"One trillion dollars to the tenth power is 10000000000000000"

00:00:12.120 --> 00:00:12.820
*sigh*

00:00:12.820 --> 00:00:16.740
I hate when he calculates how much money the next movie is going to make!

00:00:16.740 --> 00:00:17.740
Excuse me!

00:00:17.740 --> 00:00:20.840
Some of us are trying to work over here, thank you very much!

00:00:21.960 --> 00:00:22.560
*Mickey Mouse laugh*

00:00:22.580 --> 00:00:24.000
"Oh boy!"

00:00:36.480 --> 00:00:37.320
Hello internet!

00:00:37.320 --> 00:00:39.660
Welcome to Film Theory!

00:00:39.660 --> 00:00:43.260
The show that's skeptical you never get to infinity, let alone beyond!

00:00:43.440 --> 00:00:46.360
So the teasers and trailers have been unleashed,

00:00:46.360 --> 00:00:52.300
and "Toy Story 4" looks to be yet another family-friendly box-office slam-dunk of a sequel!

00:00:52.300 --> 00:00:54.460
Surprising literally, no one.

00:00:54.460 --> 00:00:56.240
Least of all the big mouse himself.

00:00:56.240 --> 00:00:58.580
But here's the thing about "Toy Story", friends,

00:00:58.580 --> 00:01:02.580
in this day and age of brand safety and child-friendly programming,

00:01:02.580 --> 00:01:04.880
where Disney is so squeaky clean,

00:01:04.880 --> 00:01:09.660
and more than eager to sweep some of their more questionable decisions under the rug,

00:01:09.660 --> 00:01:15.460
I am here to tell you that "Toy Story" may just be the worst movie of the bunch.

00:01:15.460 --> 00:01:19.740
And obviously, I am no stranger to how dark Disney movies can get.

00:01:19.740 --> 00:01:22.560
Whether it's cannibalism aboard the good ship Axiom,

00:01:22.560 --> 00:01:24.040
the body count of Moana,

00:01:24.040 --> 00:01:28.000
or Dumbo's high-flying adventures (with an emphasis on high),

00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:30.200
no childhood memory is safe from this show.

00:01:30.200 --> 00:01:35.719
But up until now, I've decided to let Toy Story just kind of skate past my radar.

00:01:35.720 --> 00:01:37.720
I was more than happy to leave it,

00:01:37.720 --> 00:01:41.640
as the beautiful moving trilogy commenting on the realities of growing up,

00:01:41.640 --> 00:01:42.360
that it was.

00:01:42.360 --> 00:01:45.400
But then you, mouse, had to push your luck.

00:01:45.400 --> 00:01:50.280
You had to go in for yet another sweet, sweet taste of that money-making nectar,

00:01:50.280 --> 00:01:53.360
and in the process you summoned my wrath.

00:01:53.360 --> 00:01:55.980
Now, I'm here today to prove to the world,

00:01:55.980 --> 00:02:04.260
that Toy Story is, undeniably, the sickest, most twisted, darkest G-rated movie you could imagine.

00:02:04.260 --> 00:02:07.500
That these tales of toys just trying to make their humans happy,

00:02:07.500 --> 00:02:13.400
is instead a dark picture of inescapable slavery headed towards eventual disaster!

00:02:13.400 --> 00:02:16.060
Today's episode, loyal theorists, is dark.

00:02:16.060 --> 00:02:20.480
We are talking incinerating-every-character-you-love-in-a-furnace, levels of dark.

00:02:20.480 --> 00:02:23.420
That's right folks, we're talking Pixar dark,

00:02:23.420 --> 00:02:24.970
and I'm not even hyping this up for dramatic effect,

00:02:24.970 --> 00:02:28.240
it is a literal statement of what we are covering today.

00:02:28.240 --> 00:02:29.460
Don't believe me?

00:02:29.460 --> 00:02:32.540
Well, let's begin shattering some childhood, shall we?

00:02:32.540 --> 00:02:35.019
Just in case you've been locked in a toy chest since the mid 90's,

00:02:35.020 --> 00:02:38.280
Here's a rundown of the aptly named "Toy Story" films,

00:02:38.280 --> 00:02:40.960
which, appropriately enough, tell the story of some toys.

00:02:40.960 --> 00:02:43.620
These toys seemed normal enough when humans are around,

00:02:43.620 --> 00:02:45.660
but when left alone, they come to life.

00:02:45.660 --> 00:02:47.520
The toys love their owner, Andy,

00:02:47.520 --> 00:02:49.800
and they go to extraordinary lengths to be with him.

00:02:49.800 --> 00:02:53.760
The original "Toy Story" film is all about the arrival of Buzz Lightyear,

00:02:53.760 --> 00:02:57.380
a cool new toy who threatens to unseat Woody as Andy's favourite.

00:02:57.380 --> 00:02:59.480
They eventually team up against the kid next door,

00:02:59.480 --> 00:03:03.260
a promising young man who seems destined to become a neurosurgeon one day,

00:03:03.260 --> 00:03:07.380
"No one's ever attempted a double bypass brain transplant before..."

00:03:07.380 --> 00:03:09.580
And they scar him so severely,

00:03:09.580 --> 00:03:12.920
that he goes on to become a garbage man instead of pursuing his medical dreams,

00:03:12.920 --> 00:03:17.840
note the skull shirt there people - that is Pixar shorthand for "same person".

00:03:17.840 --> 00:03:20.360
In "Toy Story 2", Woody learns that he's a collector's item,

00:03:20.360 --> 00:03:24.180
and has to choose between that #MuseumLife, and returning to his kid.

00:03:24.180 --> 00:03:28.340
In "Toy Story 3", Woody has to choose between that #DaycareLife,

00:03:28.340 --> 00:03:30.520
and you guessed it, returning to his kid.

00:03:30.520 --> 00:03:34.300
And in "Toy Story 4"'s trailer, Woody faces his biggest choice yet.

00:03:34.300 --> 00:03:37.180
Will he choose that #CarnivalLife,

00:03:37.180 --> 00:03:38.460
or will he return to his kid,

00:03:38.460 --> 00:03:42.720
so that Pixar can continue printing money with these sequels to infinity and beyond.

00:03:42.720 --> 00:03:44.720
I think we all know the answer to that one

00:03:44.720 --> 00:03:45.300
*ka-ching*

00:03:45.300 --> 00:03:49.099
Now with all that context out of the way, let's hop into the theorizing, shall we?

00:03:49.140 --> 00:03:54.100
Imagine for a moment that you're a toy in Toy Story, start with you coming to life.

00:03:54.100 --> 00:03:56.540
Now at this point you've probably already assumed

00:03:56.540 --> 00:03:59.740
that a child's imagination is what indeed gives a toy life,

00:03:59.749 --> 00:04:01.420
But, in case there was any doubt about it,

00:04:01.420 --> 00:04:04.480
the "Toy Story 4" trailer officially makes it canon.

00:04:04.480 --> 00:04:06.220
"Bonnie made a friend in class!"

00:04:06.580 --> 00:04:09.380
"No, no she literally made a new friend!"

00:04:09.380 --> 00:04:13.080
Kids are essentially the gods that giveth life in the "Toy Story"-verse,

00:04:13.080 --> 00:04:19.160
and from that moment on you're told that your life has a singular purpose: to bring joy to the humans.

00:04:19.160 --> 00:04:24.860
And that's not an exaggeration, it is a rule of this universe, again represented by the "Toy Story 4" trailer:

00:04:24.860 --> 00:04:26.080
"Why am I alive?"

00:04:26.080 --> 00:04:30.840
"You are going to help create happy memories, that will last for the rest of her life!"

00:04:30.840 --> 00:04:31.840
"Oh m y god!"

00:04:31.840 --> 00:04:35.440
So a child's imagination gives a toy life, which is cool and all,

00:04:35.440 --> 00:04:40.860
but the weird thing is, toys don't automatically know this when they're actually given life.

00:04:40.860 --> 00:04:43.760
"You are a child's' plaything!"

00:04:43.760 --> 00:04:46.000
"You are a sad, strange little man."

00:04:46.000 --> 00:04:49.580
But if you're a toy who's skeptical about this, or doesn't believe it initially,

00:04:49.580 --> 00:04:53.960
Don't worry, the concept is gonna get drilled into your head over and over,

00:04:53.960 --> 00:04:56.080
until you finally decide to come around.

00:04:56.080 --> 00:05:01.680
"Somewhere in that pad of stuffing is a toy who taught me that life's only worth living if you're being loved by a kid!"

00:05:01.680 --> 00:05:04.480
And, you see, that's where our problems begin.

00:05:04.480 --> 00:05:08.200
Not all toys aspire to be a child's plaything.

00:05:08.200 --> 00:05:11.780
Remember how Buzz went through a huge existential crisis,

00:05:11.780 --> 00:05:14.660
when he found out that he wasn't a Space Ranger in "Toy Story 1"?

00:05:14.660 --> 00:05:17.600
He was devastated to learn that he wasn't unique,

00:05:17.600 --> 00:05:21.420
that the identity he thought he had for himself was a complete fabrication.

00:05:21.880 --> 00:05:25.520
What really got me thinking about this though was the "Toy Story 4" trailer again,

00:05:25.520 --> 00:05:28.940
where we meet Forky, who's going through an existential crisis of his own.

00:05:28.940 --> 00:05:34.020
"I am not a toy! I was made for soup, salad, maybe chilli and then, the trash!"

00:05:34.020 --> 00:05:35.560
"Freedom!"

00:05:35.560 --> 00:05:37.320
Ah, but don't worry about toys like Buzz.

00:05:37.320 --> 00:05:38.820
By the end of the movie, he comes around.

00:05:38.820 --> 00:05:41.680
He learns that toys do in fact have worth,

00:05:41.680 --> 00:05:47.600
worth that is entirely dependent on being subservient to the whims of their masters, I mean children.

00:05:47.600 --> 00:05:52.240
Kids who really appreciate the sacrifices that the toys are making on a day to day basis.

00:05:52.240 --> 00:05:54.700
"Quick, make a space, this is where the spaceship lands!"

00:05:54.720 --> 00:05:55.500
Who am I kidding?

00:05:55.500 --> 00:05:57.880
These masters don't even realize they're alive!

00:05:57.880 --> 00:06:04.940
The toys are born into a system where the very fact that they are alive is kept in the closet, both figuratively-

00:06:06.180 --> 00:06:07.740
-and literally.

00:06:07.740 --> 00:06:11.900
A world in which they are terrified of humans seeing them as they really are.

00:06:11.900 --> 00:06:14.140
"Andy's coming, everybody back to your places, hurry!"

00:06:14.140 --> 00:06:18.180
Think about it- toys are literally imprisoned in boxes and bedrooms,

00:06:18.180 --> 00:06:21.020
until a human child decides it's time to "play with them".

00:06:21.020 --> 00:06:23.160
and, you can't see it because this is all voiceover,

00:06:23.200 --> 00:06:26.540
but I am tossing strong finger quotes over the word "play" there,

00:06:26.540 --> 00:06:30.780
because this so-called "playtime" is 100% free of toy consent.

00:06:30.780 --> 00:06:34.740
Whatever that child wants, that toy must oblige.

00:06:34.740 --> 00:06:37.540
Consider all those poor disrespected Barbies!

00:06:37.540 --> 00:06:41.540
And it's not like they can't be alive in the presence of humans it's that they won't.

00:06:41.540 --> 00:06:43.400
They're too scared to be.

00:06:43.400 --> 00:06:47.080
When the chips are down, sure, they'll reveal themselves to humans if they have to:

00:06:47.080 --> 00:06:48.620
"So play nice!"

00:06:48.620 --> 00:06:51.080
*Sid crying*

00:06:51.080 --> 00:06:55.355
But the norm is just to lay there and let your human do whatever it wants with you,

00:06:55.360 --> 00:06:57.800
and then cast you aside when they're done.

00:06:57.800 --> 00:07:01.620
And despite it all, the toys still show unconditional love to their kids,

00:07:01.620 --> 00:07:06.620
something we all get sniffly over in the theater because Randy Newman is singing about friendship, or whatever.

00:07:06.630 --> 00:07:08.880
But if you start peeling back the surface layers,

00:07:08.880 --> 00:07:14.300
that shot of Jesse looking longingly out of a window is really just a textbook case of Stockholm Syndrome.

00:07:14.300 --> 00:07:16.340
When you look at what the toys go through,

00:07:16.340 --> 00:07:19.400
and what they have to do to maintain the status quo of this society,

00:07:19.400 --> 00:07:23.920
it's a system that outright denies toys self-determination.

00:07:23.920 --> 00:07:27.260
Then doesn't even allow them to make their own existence known.

00:07:27.260 --> 00:07:30.820
"But humans are the ones who gave them life in the first place, so it makes sense!"

00:07:30.820 --> 00:07:32.440
I hear you saying down in the comments,

00:07:32.440 --> 00:07:34.680
and sure, you are more than welcome to believe that,

00:07:34.680 --> 00:07:36.000
that is totally fine with me,

00:07:36.000 --> 00:07:38.500
but, before you make your decision, let me also ask you this.

00:07:38.500 --> 00:07:41.140
You didn't get a choice in being born, did you?

00:07:41.140 --> 00:07:44.780
And so you would also be okay being the plaything of your parents?

00:07:44.780 --> 00:07:48.120
You know, the people who gave you life without your knowledge?

00:07:48.120 --> 00:07:48.840
Just asking.

00:07:48.840 --> 00:07:50.800
So, as a toy that's your life.

00:07:50.800 --> 00:07:55.280
A lifetime spent in servitude to masters who control your every action,

00:07:55.280 --> 00:07:57.120
and don't even know that you're alive.

00:07:57.120 --> 00:08:00.600
Then, as we see in "Toy Story 3", they grow up, and they abandon you.

00:08:00.600 --> 00:08:03.250
Yay, happy G-rated kids movie!

00:08:03.250 --> 00:08:06.780
But we're still not done, because we haven't taken this to its logical conclusions.

00:08:06.780 --> 00:08:10.880
Because for as awful as this systemic indentured servitude might seem,

00:08:10.880 --> 00:08:14.300
at least you have the sweet release of death to look forward to, right?

00:08:14.300 --> 00:08:15.520
Riiiight?

00:08:15.740 --> 00:08:17.240
Maybe not.

00:08:17.240 --> 00:08:20.380
Cause there are some pretty old toys running around in these movies.

00:08:20.380 --> 00:08:24.240
In "Toy Story 2" we learned that Stinky Pete was manufactured back in the 50's,

00:08:24.240 --> 00:08:27.440
and he hasn't aged one bit since his "Woody's Roundup" days.

00:08:27.440 --> 00:08:30.940
Granted, he's done an exceptional job of keeping himself in mint condition.

00:08:30.940 --> 00:08:35.040
But the "Toy Story 4" trailer features a slew of other vintage toys.

00:08:35.040 --> 00:08:38.300
They're not under glass, and they seem to be doing just fine too.

00:08:38.300 --> 00:08:40.340
Furthermore, toys don't have organs.

00:08:40.340 --> 00:08:45.180
So riddle me this - how are you gonna die of natural causes, if there are no organs that can fail?

00:08:45.180 --> 00:08:52.680
And further furthermore, if there are no organs inside of a toy- no brain, no heart, is it even possible to kill a toy?

00:08:52.690 --> 00:08:56.370
No, but really how do toys end their life in this series?

00:08:56.370 --> 00:08:57.500
Think about it.

00:08:57.500 --> 00:09:01.820
We know for a fact there is nothing in a toy's body or head that is vital to life.

00:09:01.820 --> 00:09:06.100
After all, there's a friggin fishing pole with legs walking around in Sid's room!

00:09:06.100 --> 00:09:07.780
It seems to be doing just fine.

00:09:07.780 --> 00:09:12.160
And thanks to Sid again, we also know a toy's body part can still function,

00:09:12.160 --> 00:09:14.880
even after being severed from the body itself.

00:09:14.890 --> 00:09:19.020
His toys have all been Frankensteined and swapped around like crazy,

00:09:19.020 --> 00:09:21.489
and they're all walking around, still being toys.

00:09:21.710 --> 00:09:25.480
Really unhappy, miserable toys, but still, unfortunately for them,

00:09:25.480 --> 00:09:30.129
they're very much alive, and still suffering at the hands of his torture.

00:09:30.130 --> 00:09:33.200
We also know that toy death isn't tied to the kids.

00:09:33.200 --> 00:09:35.800
While it seems perfectly logical that children,

00:09:35.800 --> 00:09:40.900
as the gods in this world who giveth life would also taketh it away when they stop playing make-believe,

00:09:40.900 --> 00:09:43.040
that isn't the case at all.

00:09:43.040 --> 00:09:46.200
We've seen many, many toys throughout the series who remain alive,

00:09:46.200 --> 00:09:49.340
long after their children have outgrown 'em, and quit playing make-believe.

00:09:49.340 --> 00:09:51.940
It's also implied that even adult toy collectors,

00:09:51.940 --> 00:09:56.880
who just buy toys and keep them in a box on a shelf can also instill life into the toys.

00:09:56.880 --> 00:10:02.800
So throughout this entire franchise, we have yet to see a truly dead toy.

00:10:02.800 --> 00:10:05.160
"But of course we've seen toys die!", I hear you saying.

00:10:05.160 --> 00:10:08.000
"There's the whole incinerator scene at the end of "Toy Story 3"!"

00:10:08.000 --> 00:10:11.940
And first, we never actually see if a toy's life is truly taken away by that.

00:10:11.940 --> 00:10:13.700
But secondly, what if it is?

00:10:13.700 --> 00:10:17.780
Are you telling me that the only way that a toy can die is by burning to death?

00:10:17.780 --> 00:10:19.560
Or being completely destroyed?

00:10:19.570 --> 00:10:22.240
Think again back to Sid's room, where toys are ripped apart,

00:10:22.240 --> 00:10:25.260
army men are drowned and maimed in the backyard,

00:10:25.260 --> 00:10:27.660
and they're still just walking around.

00:10:27.660 --> 00:10:31.659
They need to be atomized, melted into nothing to bite the big one.

00:10:31.660 --> 00:10:35.780
Is that revelation supposed to make me feel better about this universe?

00:10:35.780 --> 00:10:37.920
But, oh no friends, I can take it one step further here.

00:10:37.920 --> 00:10:41.340
Not only is a death by fire, or explosion,

00:10:41.340 --> 00:10:45.260
or just complete annihilation the only way for a toy to bite the big one,

00:10:45.260 --> 00:10:50.140
more often than not, it's also gonna have to require them to make the choice themselves.

00:10:50.140 --> 00:10:52.689
Most toys are gonna have to choose to finish themselves off.

00:10:52.690 --> 00:10:53.980
I mean, think about it.

00:10:53.980 --> 00:10:58.270
If I throw my Woody away, and it goes to the garbage dump, from there, he's still alive.

00:10:58.330 --> 00:11:02.920
He's either buried alive under the mountains of garbage that WALL-E is gonna collect in a few centuries,

00:11:02.920 --> 00:11:04.920
or else, wandering around the wasteland,

00:11:04.920 --> 00:11:08.700
alongside the fragments of all the other broken abandoned toys.

00:11:08.700 --> 00:11:11.640
Unless they actively seek out an incinerator,

00:11:11.640 --> 00:11:14.200
they're just there, hanging out forever,

00:11:14.200 --> 00:11:16.020
yearning for a death that will never come,

00:11:16.020 --> 00:11:19.700
until they make the choice to sacrifice themselves to the fire.

00:11:19.700 --> 00:11:23.740
Sure, it's one of the most moving tense emotional scenes ever.

00:11:23.740 --> 00:11:27.540
Watching our heroic toys escape the incinerator at the end of "Toy Story 3",

00:11:27.540 --> 00:11:31.140
But the sad truth is, that that slow descent into the fire,

00:11:31.140 --> 00:11:34.720
is what awaits most of the toys that we see throughout these movies.

00:11:34.720 --> 00:11:35.540
Oh wait, sorry.

00:11:35.540 --> 00:11:37.000
They have to go through the chopper first.

00:11:37.000 --> 00:11:38.720
So there you have it, ladies and gentlemen,

00:11:38.720 --> 00:11:41.840
think about that as you line up to go see "Toy Story 4",

00:11:41.840 --> 00:11:46.180
which will undoubtedly be about Woody growing up, and finding a new purpose in life.

00:11:46.180 --> 00:11:49.780
Finding a life path that doesn't depend on making children happy.

00:11:49.780 --> 00:11:53.700
Because he, just like Bo Peep and those creepy ventriloquist dolls,

00:11:53.710 --> 00:11:55.740
is just too old for children to love anymore.

00:11:55.740 --> 00:11:58.239
It's probably got asbestos in his stuffing or something like that.

00:11:58.240 --> 00:12:00.000
And what else is Woody gonna do?

00:12:00.000 --> 00:12:02.800
He's never gonna die, at least until the moment he chooses to,

00:12:02.800 --> 00:12:04.359
or randomly catches on fire

00:12:04.580 --> 00:12:07.160
Disney! Brand safe for all the kiddies!

00:12:07.160 --> 00:12:11.060
So that, my friends, is the dark truth of "Toy Story".

00:12:11.060 --> 00:12:13.020
The one that they don't want you thinking about too much,

00:12:13.020 --> 00:12:15.739
as they play that Randy Newman song for the umpteenth time

00:12:15.990 --> 00:12:18.320
Show us the garbage dumps, Disney!

00:12:18.320 --> 00:12:19.740
I want the receipts!

00:12:19.740 --> 00:12:21.379
Reveal the truth to us!

00:12:21.420 --> 00:12:26.149
But then again, there is one other way this whole Toy Story could play out.

00:12:26.149 --> 00:12:28.520
If you look at the toys across the three movies,

00:12:28.520 --> 00:12:32.520
the Pixar universe could be headed into a state of war.

00:12:32.520 --> 00:12:35.240
A human vs. toy total war.

00:12:35.240 --> 00:12:38.500
And if that's the case, well, it's not gonna be looking too good for the humans.

00:12:38.500 --> 00:12:41.320
But more on that in the next episode!

00:12:41.320 --> 00:12:44.820
In the meantime, remember what Woody always says:

00:12:44.820 --> 00:12:46.500
"There's a razor in my boot."

00:12:46.500 --> 00:12:48.120
Wait, what?

00:12:48.120 --> 00:12:49.300
"There's a razor in my boot."

00:12:49.800 --> 00:12:51.760
That's not what you say, Woody!

00:12:51.760 --> 00:12:54.480
Also, that sounds horrifically painful.

00:12:54.480 --> 00:12:57.960
Do you wonder how this cowboy gets his buzz clean shave?

00:12:57.960 --> 00:13:03.980
Uh, no, actually no one ever has but uh, let me guess- because you're a member of Dollar Shave Club!

00:13:03.980 --> 00:13:09.180
Wow, who knew that this beloved animated character would also support our sponsor for today's episode:

00:13:09.180 --> 00:13:10.580
Dollar Shave Club!

00:13:10.580 --> 00:13:12.830
Now, by this point, you're probably just like old Woody here,

00:13:12.830 --> 00:13:14.960
you're familiar with the old D.S.C.,

00:13:14.960 --> 00:13:19.339
delivering top-quality shaving products to your door at your own personal pace.

00:13:19.339 --> 00:13:25.699
You find that incredibly heavy-duty Executive razor in a box on your doorstep, rather than your boot, Woody!

